; newworlds.eval - the three ways to make a world (editor-updates P4).
;
; Made from dungeon-demo, with an UNSAVED edit in hand first (a 3x3 of
; floor_slabs on eval_arena), so the judge (tools/EditorTest.py phase 9) can
; see the copy carry it while dungeon-demo's own file stays as it was:
;   nw_blank   the template's content and one starter room with an exit
;   nw_copy    this world whole, the unsaved edit included
;   nw_level   dungeon-demo's content and crypt1 alone, its stairs replaced
;              by one exit
; then each refusal, in its own words. The judge opens each world with
; -project and runs worldcheck.eval there, and removes them all after.

logecho on
reset
editor fill floors floor_slabs rect 3 3 5 5
worlds new nw_blank
worlds new nw_copy copy
worlds new nw_level level crypt1
echo --- refusals ---
worlds new nw_blank
worlds new !!!
worlds new nw_bad level nowhere
worlds
